course: dictionary
lesson: 14321
title: Naming the player
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An oboist is a person who plays the oboe. Many words for players end in -ist: a pianist plays the piano, and a violinist plays the violin. Once you know the instrument, you can work out the player.
explain: «The oboist played a clear, sweet note before the concert began.» The clue is played. Someone played a note, and the word before the instrument tells you who it was. Ask yourself: who did the playing? That is the oboist.
explain: «In the orchestra, the oboist played the note A, and everyone tuned their instruments to it.» Tuned is a clue. The other players match their sound to the oboist's note, so the oboist helps the whole group sound right together.
fact: An oboist is a person who plays the oboe.
fact: The oboe is a woodwind instrument with a double reed, two thin reeds that vibrate together to make the sound.
fact: The word «oboist» comes from «oboe», so the word tells you which instrument the player uses.
fact: In an orchestra, the oboist often plays the note A, and the other players tune to it.
fact: Other players end in -ist too: a pianist plays the piano, and a violinist plays the violin.
exercise: «The oboist played a clear, sweet note before the concert began.» What is an oboist? | A large drum in the orchestra | A person who sells tickets for concerts | A room where concerts are held | *A person who plays the oboe
exercise: In an orchestra, the oboist often plays a note that the others tune to. Which note is it? | A drum beat | The last note of the song | A loud shout | *The note A
exercise: An oboist plays a special instrument. Which instrument is it? | Violin | Flute | *Oboe | Trumpet
test: «My neighbour is an oboist, and she practises every evening.» What does oboist mean? | A person who builds houses | *A person who plays the oboe | A person who runs a shop | A person who paints pictures
test: Why does the oboist's note matter in an orchestra? | Because it is the loudest sound | Because it ends the concert | Because it tells the audience to clap | *Because the other players tune to it
exam: Which sentence uses oboist correctly? | The oboist ate a sandwich in the park | The oboist parked the car by the school | *The oboist played a sweet note on her oboe at the concert | The oboist washed the dishes after tea
